        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(workboard): share Control UI contract",
        "body": "Related: #102258\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Control UI maintained a separate copy of the Workboard card and metadata contract. Changes to plugin-owned fields could silently drift or be dropped by the UI, including diagnostic actions, notification sequence values, and workspace source metadata.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis moves the canonical Workboard data model to the supported `@openclaw/workboard/contract.js` package seam and makes both plugin internals and the Control UI consume it. UI-only lifecycle, task, refresh, and presentation state remains local to the Control UI.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no intended visual behavior change. Workboard metadata now follows one package-owned contract, reducing silent UI drift and preserving plugin-owned fields across gateway normalization.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox `tbx_01kx1ayeeq603djks62f5gevcb`: 181 Control UI Workboard tests and 6 Workboard gateway tests passed.\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox `tbx_01kx1ayeeq603djks62f5gevcb`: `pnpm ui:build` passed.\n- Fresh Testbox-through-Crabbox `tbx_01kx1b9w1t57v2epzzqmzn54nx`: explicit path-scoped `pnpm check:changed` passed, including TSGo, oxlint, shrinkwrap guards, runtime sidecar checks, and import-cycle validation.\n- Codex autoreview (`gpt-5.5`, high): clean with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n",
